# No AI co-authors on commits

Never attribute commits to an AI model, coding agent, or assistant.

## Required

- Commit messages must not include any `Co-authored-by` trailer for Cursor, Claude, Composer, GPT, Copilot, or any other AI/agent identity.
- Do not add `Signed-off-by`, `Assisted-by`, `Generated-by`, or similar trailers that credit an AI/agent.
- If the environment or a hook injects an AI co-author trailer, strip it before push (amend or rewrite the message, then push). Confirm with `git log -1 --format='%B'` that no AI co-author line remains.
- Human co-authors are allowed only when the user explicitly asks to add a specific person.

## Examples

```text
# Bad
feat(events): add server-side pagination to admin table

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
```

```text
# Good
feat(events): add server-side pagination to admin table
```
